With the below spec, running in vega-lite mode on https://vega.github.io/editor/ no data plot is shown, except the legend title (`Unemployment (%)`) and a warning `[Warning] Infinite extent for field "percentage": [Infinity, -Infinity]`.

When I remove the `"layer": [{ ... }]` part, leaving only the top-level spec, the plot succeeds without warning. I've compared the generated Vega specs between the cases and don't immediately see something obvious causing this, but as the Vega spec when the layer is set also shows nothing I must be missing what is going on.

Looking at other layered plot examples, such as https://vega.github.io/vega-lite/examples/geo_layer.html, I think I'm doing the layer setup correct, right?

```json
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "width": 600,
  "height": 400,
  "layer": [
    {
     "data": {
        "url": "data/us-10m.json",
        "format": {
          "type": "topojson",
          "feature": "counties"
        }
      },
      "transform": [
        {
          "lookup": "id",
          "from": {
            "data": {
              "url": "data/unemployment.tsv"
            },
            "key": "id",
            "fields": ["rate"]
          }
        },
        {"calculate": "datum.rate*100", "as": "percentage"}
      ],
      "projection": {
        "type": "albersUsa"
      },
      "mark": "geoshape",
      "encoding": {
        "color": {
          "field": "percentage",
          "type": "quantitative",
          "bin": {"step": 5.0},
          "scale": {
            "range": ["#e0e0e0", "#c0c0c0", "gold", "darkorange", "red", "purple", "black"]
          },
          "title": "Unemployment (%)"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

