Where the vega-lite specification should be defined similar to this [Open the Chart in the Vega Editor](https://vega.github.io/editor/#/url/vega--daJFQ0bZIXa5ZTPQ65QHAwbDPKVKD+cY0ZT0NAARjEpyU8Bo5mKCtOKtBh2OyJAKVF6DBnyUyG0Nn0TG8uWarXasjI-n6JWMY3m-iZLOKIHZ8nFTGq-mQvSD8LQVlOkRArxKSDIZCZFCxftxNXCShWLn89VWaQAxAA2EvhSKgWG8hEuBAG92CWr+aKxa2ZbJlhkWq3oG3aO0tNodF3+d3PZRe5lwVnof2Z9LBkqh8NdKMxuOgBNJvip1oMDPi7N9kp5hhpFy8sh0iJDMJAA) as is mentioned in this [comment](https://github.com/vega/vega-lite/issues/8348#issuecomment-1280162030)

Which contains a `params` definition as follows:
```json
"params": [
  {
    "name": "brush",
    "select": {"type": "interval", "encodings": ["x"]},
    "views": [
      ["child__column_distance", "layer_0"],
      ["child__column_delay", "layer_0"],
      ["child__column_time", "layer_0"]
    ]
  }
],
```
Where our definition looks as such:
```
"params": [
  {
    "name": "param_26",
    "select": {
      "encodings": [
        "x"
      ],
      "type": "interval"
    },
    "views": [
      "view_29"
    ]
  }
]
```
The `views` object is different. 

