Hello 👋 ! I believe I found an issue in VegaLite's generation of Vega `signals` when binding to field's with escaped names.

# Demonstration

The following is a simple example of a chart using a select `param` on the `x` encoding to mark bars as red when clicked.
[Link to Vega Editor](https://vega.github.io/editor/#/url/vega-).

```json
{
  "data": {
    "values": [
      { "category": "A", "value": 10 },
      { "category": "B", "value": 15 },
      { "category": "C", "value": 12 }
    ]
  },
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "category",
      "type": "nominal",
      "axis": { "labelAngle": 0 }
    },
    "y": { "field": "value", "type": "quantitative" },
    "color": {
      "condition": {
        "param": "bar_click",
        "value": "red",
        "empty": false
      },
      "value": "blue"
    }
  },
  "params": [
    { "name": "bar_click", "select": { "type": "point", "encodings": ["x"] } }
  ]
}
```

The above works correctly.

However, if we modify the x axis to require escaping the field name (changing `category` -> `cat.egory`), then anytime we click a bar, we get an internal error in the console (`[Error] Cannot read properties of undefined (reading '0')`). The selection is never filled with values.
[Link to Vega Editor](https://vega.github.io/editor/#/url/vega--BAAte6vio212+2k9yqBCgcXaXXoHQo4Wh5yCIXCZB+IFiTj4TiAA).

```json
{
  "data": {
    "values": [
      { "cat.egory": "A", "value": 10 },
      { "cat.egory": "B", "value": 15 },
      { "cat.egory": "C", "value": 12 },
      { "cat.egory": "D", "value": 20 }
    ]
  },
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "field": "cat\\.egory",
      "axis": { "labelAngle": 0 }
    },
    "y": { "field": "value", "type": "quantitative" },
    "color": {
      "condition": {
        "param": "bar_click",
        "value": "red",
        "empty": false
      },
      "value": "blue"
    }
  },
  "params": [
    { "name": "bar_click", "select": { "type": "point", "encodings": ["x"] } }
  ]
}
```

# Investigation

Looking at the difference between the two resultant Vega specs, the issue appears to be within VegaLite.

The following is the update expression (`signals.bar_click_tuple.on[0]`) for the incorrect example:

```json
{
  "update": "datum && item().mark.marktype !== 'group' && indexof(item().mark.role, 'legend') < 0 ? {unit: \"\", fields: bar_click_tuple_fields, values: [(item().isVoronoi ? datum.datum : datum)[\"cat\\\\.egory\"]]} : null"
},
```

Zooming in on the last section (since this is a looong expression) we can see that we attempt to access a `datum` at a double-escaped field name:

```json
"(item().isVoronoi ? datum.datum : datum)[\"cat\\\\.egory\"]"
```

This seems to indicate that the signal generation logic re-escapes an already escaped field name, leading to a brand new name being indexed on (leading to looking for `cat\.egory` instead of `cat.egory`).

If you modify the Vega spec and only change this one access to either a single-escaped version (`[\"cat.egory\"]`) or a no-escaped version (`[\"cat\\.egory\"]`) you get a working example.
