# Workaround

For anyone else who runs into this in case this issue becomes dead or proves too difficult to fix for some reason.

Currently, our team works around this issue by looking into the generated Vega spec, inspecting any and all `signal` definitions, and using a regex to patch the double escape pattern back to a sensible value. We only do this on the signals that match a pattern our code generates, so the below might not capture all signals:
```ts
const DOUBLE_ESCAPED = /(\["[^"]*)\\\\([^"]*"\])/g;
function fixSignalEscape(spec: VegaSpec) {
  if (!spec.signals) return;
  for (const signal of spec.signals) {
    if (!signal.name.endsWith("_tuple")) continue;
    for (const onEvent of signal.on ?? []) {
      if (
        !("update" in onEvent) ||
        !onEvent.update ||
        typeof onEvent.update !== "string"
      )
        continue;
      const updateExpr = onEvent.update;
      const fixedExpr = updateExpr.replace(DOUBLE_ESCAPED, "$1$2");
      onEvent.update = fixedExpr;
    }
  }
}
```

