`domain` is used to set the range of a scale. However, using it with a binned  scale leads to the unexpected result of the bins not being recalculated and the axis ticks not extending all the way to the edges of the axis (which is the case in all other contexts `domain` is used), creating an odd empty space:

```json
{
  "data": {"url": "data/movies.json"},
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "bin": true,
      "field": "IMDB Rating",
      "scale": {"domain": [0, 20]}
    },
    "y": {"aggregate": "count"}
  }
}
```

![image](https://github.com/vega/vega-lite/assets/4560057/6ade032e-1392-4b75-b444-b801a663d77a)

Instead, when working with binned scales, the `extent` of the `bin` parameter needs to be set to achieve the expected result:

```json
{
  "data": {"url": "data/movies.json"},
  "mark": "bar",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {
      "bin": {"extent": [0, 20]},
      "field": "IMDB Rating",
    },
    "y": {"aggregate": "count"}
  }
}
```

![image](https://github.com/vega/vega-lite/assets/4560057/8243e204-5321-41e1-b37e-2dd5dfdfbe64)

Effectively this means that for changing the range of an axis, there is one default method (`domain`) that works with all charts except those with binned scales which is a special case where a separate method needs to be used (`extent`). I find this inconvenient and a common point of confusion when teaching with Altair.

A solution would be that when setting the `domain` of a binned scale, the `extent` is set to the same value (unless it is already manually set to another value). This means that the same mental model can be used to change the axis ranges of all charts. This would also allow for the use of `resolve_scale` to unify the extents/scales of multiple binned scales, which is currently not possible.

There is some previous discussion of this in https://github.com/vega/vega-lite/issues/2791 and https://github.com/vega/vega-lite/issues/3575. @kanitw made a similar comment in https://github.com/vega/vega-lite/issues/2791#issuecomment-323247255 pointing out the weird empty space from setting only `domain` on a binned field and mentioning that "...I think extent and domain should be the same value..." (although this was a long time ago now).

This was originally reported in https://github.com/hex-inc/vegafusion/issues/381, but it appears to be a Vega-Lite issue.  Given this grouped density Vega-Lite spec:

